WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.078 --> 00:00:04.328
Inside the park Ally began scanning people's minds.

2
00:00:04.329 --> 00:00:09.191
Mateo kept trying to hurry her along.

3
00:00:09.192 --> 00:00:14.102
"Hmm, people are mostly thinking about the eclipse," Ally said.

4
00:00:14.103 --> 00:00:20.883
"Ally, Mateo!" Julius waved to them from across the green. "Over here!"

5
00:00:20.884 --> 00:00:27.951
Ally and Mateo went over to their friends' blanket.

6
00:00:27.952 --> 00:00:30.663
"Sorry we're late," Mateo said.

7
00:00:30.664 --> 00:00:33.796
"We got a text from Barry that made us worried.

8
00:00:33.797 --> 00:00:39.311
We think someone is spying on us and sharing our recipes with the other teams."

9
00:00:39.312 --> 00:00:41.793
Bethany looked stunned.

10
00:00:41.794 --> 00:00:45.901
"Whoa! Who are the possible suspects?" Julius asked.

11
00:00:45.902 --> 00:00:49.686
As they ate, Mateo answered Julius' question.

12
00:00:49.687 --> 00:00:53.761
"It's got to be someone who spends a lot of time at the diner.

13
00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:56.658
I doubt it's Randy or Phil."

14
00:00:56.659 --> 00:01:01.322
"And Flo would never spy on us," Ally said.

15
00:01:01.323 --> 00:01:06.837
"Ooh!" Bethany gasped. "The eclipse is starting."

16
00:01:06.838 --> 00:01:08.669
Ally looked up.

17
00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:12.609
The moon was turning a beautiful red color.

18
00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:17.398
She felt a chill go up her spine, and goosebumps appeared on her arms.

19
00:01:17.399 --> 00:01:21.338
"It reminds me of Zorgab 8!" Ally cried.

20
00:01:21.339 --> 00:01:24.238
Julius looked at her, confused.

21
00:01:24.239 --> 00:01:28.788
"Never mind! Ha-ha! That's an old joke."

22
00:01:28.789 --> 00:01:33.093
Julius laughed and nodded, but he still looked confused.

23
00:01:33.094 --> 00:01:35.122
"Ugh!" Ally thought.

24
00:01:35.123 --> 00:01:38.043
"What is he thinking about me right now?

25
00:01:38.044 --> 00:01:42.354
Probably that I'm weird, and he'll never date me again!"

26
00:01:42.355 --> 00:01:46.494
She tried to read Julius' mind, but she couldn't hear any thoughts.

27
00:01:46.495 --> 00:01:50.728
Instead all she heard was a buzzing sound, like static.

28
00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:54.135
She was about to try again when Julius looked at her.

29
00:01:54.136 --> 00:01:58.166
"I'm glad you're here." He smiled.

30
00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:02.566
Ally smiled back, forgetting to worry about his thoughts.

31
00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:09.803
Instead she watched his smile—and the bright red moon above.

32
00:02:09.804 --> 00:02:15.019
After the eclipse the kids started packing up their picnic.

33
00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.315
"That was amazing!" Julius said.

34
00:02:18.316 --> 00:02:22.072
"It makes me want to learn more about the moon and space stuff."

35
00:02:22.073 --> 00:02:26.189
Mateo grinned. "Ally's a space expert.

36
00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:31.373
Hey, Ally. You should take Julius to the UFO museum."

37
00:02:31.374 --> 00:02:33.978
"How about tomorrow?" Julius said.

38
00:02:33.979 --> 00:02:38.350
Ally blushed. "Okay."

39
00:02:38.351 --> 00:02:42.082
"Do you two want to come?" Julius asked Mateo and Bethany.

40
00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:46.411
Mateo shrugged. "We have plans. Right, Bethany?"

41
00:02:46.412 --> 00:02:49.300
"Yep." Bethany nodded.

42
00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:54.086
"Hmm," Ally thought. "Why is Julius inviting them?

43
00:02:54.087 --> 00:02:56.943
Maybe he doesn't want to be alone with me."

44
00:02:56.944 --> 00:03:01.359
She tried to read Julius' mind again, but it didn't work.

45
00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.478
"That's so strange," Ally thought.

46
00:03:04.479 --> 00:03:07.687
"Maybe—" Suddenly something caught her eye.

47
00:03:07.688 --> 00:03:11.702
Across the green Flo was talking to a woman.

48
00:03:11.703 --> 00:03:16.493
"Flo!" Ally waved, but Flo just stared at her blankly.

49
00:03:16.494 --> 00:03:20.706
Then Flo and the woman fled the park.

50
00:03:20.707 --> 00:03:23.462
"Who was that, Ally?" Julius asked.

51
00:03:23.463 --> 00:03:25.990
"Flo. She works at the diner.

52
00:03:25.991 --> 00:03:28.407
I think she's mad at me."

53
00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:32.846
Julius shrugged. "She looked like she didn't want to be seen or something.

54
00:03:32.847 --> 00:03:35.109
Maybe she's the mole."

55
00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:40.875
"No way," Mateo said. "Flo and Papi are close."

56
00:03:40.876 --> 00:03:44.085
"I read a lot of spy novels," Julius said.

57
00:03:44.086 --> 00:03:47.090
"Spies are trained to get close."

58
00:03:47.091 --> 00:03:48.743
Ally shook her head.

59
00:03:48.744 --> 00:03:56.750
"There's no way Flo is the mole—and I'll prove it tomorrow at work."

60
00:03:56.751 --> 00:04:01.077
The next day Ally kept trying to talk to Flo.

61
00:04:01.078 --> 00:04:06.270
But the diner was so busy, she finally decided to try reading Flo's mind.

62
00:04:06.271 --> 00:04:09.095
Reading minds had always been easy for Ally.

63
00:04:09.096 --> 00:04:11.497
She'd never had to think about what to do.

64
00:04:11.498 --> 00:04:15.171
But today was different.

65
00:04:15.172 --> 00:04:20.400
Whenever she tried to hear Flo's thoughts, all she heard was static.

66
00:04:20.401 --> 00:04:23.171
"It's like I forgot how to do it."

67
00:04:23.172 --> 00:04:28.106
Ally turned, trying to read the thoughts of a few customers.

68
00:04:28.107 --> 00:04:32.524
"Oh no!" She started to panic when she heard the static again.

69
00:04:32.525 --> 00:04:37.407
"Something's wrong with me!" Suddenly something occurred to her.

70
00:04:37.408 --> 00:04:40.657
"Maybe Alpha is right.

71
00:04:40.658 --> 00:04:45.263
Maybe I am becoming too human!"

72
00:04:45.264 --> 00:04:50.153
At the end of the lunch rush, Ally finally got a chance to talk to Flo.

73
00:04:50.154 --> 00:04:53.187
"So . . . " She kept her voice light.

74
00:04:53.188 --> 00:04:58.084
"Did you hear another food truck is making chocolate hand pies?"

75
00:04:58.085 --> 00:05:00.201
"No," Flo said.

76
00:05:00.202 --> 00:05:05.005
"It's the second time that another team seemed to steal our idea."

77
00:05:05.006 --> 00:05:06.722
She shook her head.

78
00:05:06.723 --> 00:05:11.167
"It's almost like someone is giving away our secrets."

79
00:05:11.168 --> 00:05:16.090
"Huh." Flo shrugged and walked away.

80
00:05:16.091 --> 00:05:22.782
"Flo doesn't even seem to care," Ally thought as Barry arrived.

81
00:05:22.783 --> 00:05:27.458
"Hey, Ally." Barry yawned.

82
00:05:27.459 --> 00:05:33.083
"I was up all night, but I finally came up with a recipe that no one else will think of.

83
00:05:33.084 --> 00:05:37.022
Mateo is going to meet me at the food truck later to test it out. It's—"

84
00:05:37.023 --> 00:05:41.728
Ally slapped her hand over his mouth. "Don't say it out loud!"

85
00:05:41.729 --> 00:05:44.623
"Why not?" Barry mumbled.

86
00:05:44.624 --> 00:05:50.447
Ally glanced around before releasing her hand. "It's not safe!"

87
00:05:50.448 --> 00:05:53.514
"Okay." Barry nodded.

88
00:05:53.515 --> 00:05:57.619
"I'll keep this recipe close to my chest."

89
00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:11.906
Ally frowned. "Won't that get messy?"

